<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Vicenza</h1><p class="st-meta">1147 CE – 1311 CE (approx.) · capital Vicenza</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Veneto city-republic that founded a short-lived university and spent much of its history under the rule of stronger neighbours.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a>, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Padua</a>, had consuls by 1147 after its citizens took power from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>. It joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veronese-league">Veronese League</a> in 1164 and then the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The commune was governed by consuls and later a podestà. A university was founded in 1204 but soon faded. From the 1230s the city came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezzelino-iii-da-romano">Ezzelino III da Romano</a>, and after his fall <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Padua</a> controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a> from 1266. Wool and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> were its main trades, and its noble families held castles in the surrounding hills and the Berici hills to the south. Like its neighbours, it was split by feuds between Guelph and Ghibelline families.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1311 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cangrande-i-della-scala">Cangrande della Scala</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a>, and it became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-verona">Lordship of Verona</a>. In 1404 it submitted to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a>, which ruled it until 1797.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1147 CE – 1311 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.53%;width:3.26%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1147 CE – 1311 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vicenza</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Venetian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vicenza</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1229&amp;focus=commune-of-vicenza" aria-label="Commune of Vicenza on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4954 572 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Vicenza lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5274 828L5261 831M5274 828L5293 831"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5261 831h0M5293 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5274 828h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5274 828h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vicenza. <a href="/atlas?year=1229&amp;focus=commune-of-vicenza">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

